### ⚠️ Risk Assessment

A formal risk assessment was conducted across the system to identify threats, evaluate their likelihood and impact, and apply appropriate mitigations.

**Risk Register — TechCorp Berlin IT Infrastructure:**

| Risk ID | Risk Description | Likelihood | Impact | Risk Level | Mitigation Applied |
|---------|-----------------|-----------|--------|------------|-------------------|
| R-01 | Unauthorised access to IMAP mailbox via brute force | High | High | 🔴 Critical | Fail2ban jail — 5 attempts = 1hr ban |
| R-02 | Email intercepted in transit (no encryption) | Medium | High | 🟠 High | TLS enabled on Postfix (SMTP) and Dovecot (IMAP port 993) |
| R-03 | Production database loss due to backup failure | Low | Critical | 🔴 Critical | Daily automated backup + alert on failure |
| R-04 | SLA breach causing customer dissatisfaction | Medium | Medium | 🟡 Medium | Hourly SLA monitoring script + escalation triggers |
| R-05 | Disk space exhaustion causing service outage | Medium | High | 🟠 High | Daily disk check in morning-check.sh + storage ticket at 89% |
| R-06 | Unauthorised ticket access by wrong agent | Low | Medium | 🟡 Medium | Role-based access control — agents only see their group tickets |
| R-07 | Personal data retained beyond legal limit | Low | High | 🟠 High | DSGVO retention script — 90-day auto-close, 30-day backup purge |
| R-08 | Single point of failure — all services on one host | High | Critical | 🔴 Critical | Documented as known lab limitation; in production, services would be separated |
| R-09 | Weak or default credentials on mail accounts | Medium | High | 🟠 High | Strong password policy enforced in Dovecot passwd file |
| R-10 | Undetected service outage | Medium | High | 🟠 High | Morning health check script monitors all services daily |

**Risk appetite:** In this lab environment, high-availability and hardware redundancy risks (R-08) are accepted as known limitations of a single-VM homelab. In a production deployment, these would be mitigated through clustering and offsite replication.

