### 📋 Compliance

The lab is designed to comply with three major compliance frameworks relevant to German IT environments:

#### 🇪🇺 DSGVO (Datenschutz-Grundverordnung / GDPR)

DSGVO compliance was implemented across the entire data lifecycle:

| DSGVO Article | Requirement | Implementation |
|--------------|-------------|----------------|
| Art. 5(1)(e) — Storage limitation | Personal data not kept longer than necessary | Tickets auto-closed after 90 days; backups purged after 30 days via `zammad-retention.sh` |
| Art. 5(1)(f) — Integrity & confidentiality | Data protected against unauthorised access | TLS encryption on all mail transport; Fail2ban blocking brute force |
| Art. 32 — Security of processing | Appropriate technical measures | TLS, Fail2ban, role-based access control, encrypted backup |
| Art. 25 — Data protection by design | Privacy built into the system from the start | Minimal data collected in tickets; auto-close removes stale personal data |
| Art. 5(1)(b) — Purpose limitation | Data used only for its original purpose | Ticket data used only for IT support; no third-party sharing |

The weekly retention script (`zammad-retention.sh`) enforces data minimisation automatically:

```bash
# Closes open tickets older than 90 days
old_open = Ticket.where(state: open).where('created_at < ?', 90.days.ago)
# Purges backups older than 30 days
find $BACKUP_DIR -type f -mtime +30 -delete
```

#### 🛡️ BSI Grundschutz (German Federal Office for Information Security)

The BSI IT-Grundschutz baseline was applied to all components:

| BSI Module | Control | Implementation |
|-----------|---------|----------------|
| APP.5.3 — Postfix | Secure SMTP configuration | TLS enforced, weak protocols disabled (`!SSLv2, !SSLv3, !TLSv1, !TLSv1.1`) |
| APP.5.3 — Dovecot | Secure IMAP configuration | TLS on port 993, passwd-file authentication |
| OPS.1.1.3 — Patch management | Systems kept up to date | Ubuntu 22.04 LTS with automatic security updates |
| OPS.1.1.5 — Data backup | Regular automated backups | Daily backup covering DB, files, and mail config |
| DER.2.1 — Incident handling | Structured incident response | L1/L2/L3 escalation path with documented procedures |
| ORP.4 — Identity management | Role-based access control | Agent, Admin, IT-Supervisor, Security-Analyst, Team-Lead roles |

#### ✅ ITIL v4 Compliance

| ITIL Practice | Implementation |
|--------------|----------------|
| Incident Management | Three-tier ticket routing with SLA enforcement and formal escalation |
| Problem Management | Root cause documented in ticket notes (e.g. VPN hardware fault investigation) |
| Change Management | All configuration changes tested and documented before deployment |
| Service Level Management | Three SLA tiers with automated monitoring and breach alerting |
| Service Desk | Zammad as the single point of contact for all IT requests |
