## 🔍 Threat Modelling

Threat modelling was applied to the TechCorp Berlin infrastructure using two industry-standard frameworks: **STRIDE** for identifying security threats against system components, and **LINDDUN** for identifying privacy threats against personal data processed by the ticketing system. This dual approach reflects both security and DSGVO obligations simultaneously.

---

### 🧱 System Decomposition — Data Flow Diagram

Before applying any threat model, the system was decomposed into its core components and data flows:

```
┌─────────────┐     SMTP/TLS      ┌─────────────┐     IMAP/TLS     ┌─────────────┐
│   External  │ ───────────────▶  │   Postfix   │ ──────────────▶  │   Dovecot   │
│   Senders   │                   │    (MTA)    │                   │   (IMAP)    │
└─────────────┘                   └─────────────┘                   └──────┬──────┘
                                                                           │
                                                                    Poll mailbox
                                                                           │
┌─────────────┐    REST API       ┌─────────────┐                   ┌──────▼──────┐
│  IT Admins  │ ◀──────────────▶  │   Zammad    │ ◀──────────────── │  helpdesk@  │
│  & Agents   │                   │  (Tickets)  │                   │  mailbox    │
└─────────────┘                   └──────┬──────┘                   └─────────────┘
                                         │
                                  PostgreSQL DB
                                         │
                                  ┌──────▼──────┐
                                  │  Ticket &   │
                                  │  User Data  │
                                  └─────────────┘
```

**Trust Boundaries identified:**
- External internet → Postfix (SMTP boundary)
- Postfix → Dovecot (internal mail boundary)
- Dovecot → Zammad (IMAP polling boundary)
- Zammad → PostgreSQL (application-database boundary)
- Admin browser → Zammad REST API (authentication boundary)

