### ⚔️ STRIDE Threat Model

STRIDE was applied component-by-component across the entire stack. Each threat category was evaluated against each system component to identify attack vectors and verify mitigations.

**STRIDE Categories:**
- **S** — Spoofing identity
- **T** — Tampering with data
- **R** — Repudiation
- **I** — Information disclosure
- **D** — Denial of service
- **E** — Elevation of privilege

#### Postfix (SMTP Mail Transfer Agent)

| Threat | Category | Description | Mitigation | Status |
|--------|----------|-------------|-----------|--------|
| Email sender spoofing | **S** | Attacker sends email appearing to be from `admin@techcorp-berlin.de` | SPF/DKIM records recommended for production; TLS verifies transport | ⚠️ Partial |
| Mail queue tampering | **T** | Attacker modifies queued messages before delivery | Postfix queue files owned by root; restricted filesystem permissions | ✅ Mitigated |
| No mail delivery logging | **R** | No evidence of who sent what and when | `/var/log/mail.log` records all SMTP transactions with timestamps | ✅ Mitigated |
| Plaintext SMTP interception | **I** | Email content readable in transit | TLS enforced with `smtpd_tls_security_level = may`; weak protocols disabled | ✅ Mitigated |
| SMTP flood / open relay abuse | **D** | Attacker floods mail queue causing outage | Postfix relay restrictions; Fail2ban `postfix` jail active | ✅ Mitigated |
| Postfix running as root | **E** | Process compromise leads to full system access | Postfix drops privileges to `postfix` user after binding port 25 | ✅ Mitigated |

#### Dovecot (IMAP Server)

| Threat | Category | Description | Mitigation | Status |
|--------|----------|-------------|-----------|--------|
| Credential brute force | **S** | Attacker guesses IMAP passwords to access mailboxes | Fail2ban `dovecot` jail — 5 attempts = 1hr ban | ✅ Mitigated |
| Mailbox file tampering | **T** | Local attacker modifies mail files in `/var/mail/vhosts/` | Files owned by `vmail` user; access restricted | ✅ Mitigated |
| Failed login attempts not logged | **R** | No record of authentication failures | Dovecot logs all auth failures to `/var/log/mail.log` | ✅ Mitigated |
| IMAP credentials in cleartext | **I** | Password exposed during login on unencrypted connection | TLS enforced on port 993; verified with `openssl s_client` | ✅ Mitigated |
| IMAP service crash | **D** | Malformed IMAP commands crash Dovecot | Systemd auto-restart configured; monitored via `morning-check.sh` | ✅ Mitigated |
| Dovecot misconfiguration allowing any login | **E** | Disabled system auth bypassed | System auth explicitly disabled; only passwd-file auth active | ✅ Mitigated |

#### Zammad (Ticketing Application)

| Threat | Category | Description | Mitigation | Status |
|--------|----------|-------------|-----------|--------|
| API token theft | **S** | Stolen token used to impersonate admin via REST API | Tokens scoped to minimum required permissions; stored server-side | ✅ Mitigated |
| Ticket data manipulation via API | **T** | Attacker modifies ticket content or assignments via API | Token authorization required for all write operations; 403 on unauthorised | ✅ Mitigated |
| Admin actions not attributed | **R** | No record of who changed ticket state or assigned agents | Full audit trail in Zammad Activity Stream; all actions attributed to user ID | ✅ Mitigated |
| Ticket data accessible without auth | **I** | Unauthenticated API access to customer data | All API endpoints require token; tested and confirmed 401 without token | ✅ Mitigated |
| Ticket flood causing outage | **D** | Attacker floods helpdesk with spam tickets | Email-based ticket creation rate limited by Postfix; manual review possible | ⚠️ Partial |
| Agent accessing other group tickets | **E** | L1 agent reads L3-Sysadmin confidential tickets | Group-based access control — agents only see tickets in their assigned groups | ✅ Mitigated |

#### PostgreSQL (Database)

| Threat | Category | Description | Mitigation | Status |
|--------|----------|-------------|-----------|--------|
| Database connection spoofing | **S** | Attacker impersonates Zammad to connect to DB | DB listens only on localhost; no external access | ✅ Mitigated |
| SQL injection via ticket fields | **T** | Malicious input in ticket body alters DB queries | Zammad uses ActiveRecord ORM with parameterised queries | ✅ Mitigated |
| No DB query logging | **R** | No evidence of suspicious queries | PostgreSQL logging enabled; Zammad logs all DB interactions | ✅ Mitigated |
| Database dump accessible | **I** | Backup file readable by unauthorised user | Backup files owned by root; stored in `/var/backups/zammad/` with restricted permissions | ✅ Mitigated |
| DB crash due to disk full | **D** | Full disk causes PostgreSQL to crash | Daily disk check in `morning-check.sh`; storage ticket raised at 89% capacity | ✅ Mitigated |
| DB user with excessive privileges | **E** | Zammad DB user can drop tables or access other DBs | Zammad DB user scoped to `zammad` database only | ✅ Mitigated |

